+# PrintCheck — canonical state for 3.4.0-alpha48
+
+This file is the in-source handoff. Do not simplify or reset the project when continuing development.
+
+## Product goal
+PrintCheck is a standalone Android application for a technical designer. It signs in to gifts.ru only through the site session, reads order data in read-only mode, downloads order layouts/templates, proves the selected application field, extracts the actual artwork, checks that artwork against the technical requirements of the selected application, and presents a designer-friendly evidence report.
+
+## Binding processing order
+1. Read order / item / selected application / place / printing method and technical requirements.
+2. Download the layout and every related template/reference while retaining original and local file names.
+3. Prove the selected field from a real constructor/template object. Order dimensions/name are verification/scoring only and must never create a synthetic field.
+4. Register constructor/template to layout. Deleted constructor fragments are allowed and are not artwork.
+5. Extract only the residual artwork inside the proved field.
+6. Calibrate physical scale from the real field before measuring artwork and small elements.
+7. Check the artwork only against the requirements of the selected application/printing method.
+8. When evidence is insufficient or ambiguous, return manual review instead of a false OK.
+
+## Geometry and artwork constraints
+- The constructor is auxiliary evidence; the selected application and its technical requirements are authoritative for what must be checked.
+- Partial removal of constructor/template content from a production layout is not an error.
+- Dotted/technical field frames are template geometry, not artwork.
+- Guard field is measured to all four real field edges. Exact threshold passes; smaller distance fails; outside-field distance is negative and fails.
+- Artwork dimensions and field dimensions are physical W×H in mm.
+- Evidence overlays use dynamic outline width so small applications are not obscured.
+
+## Small positive / negative elements
+- Analyze each stable visible color layer separately.
+- Positive = physical width of an object/stroke/letter of one color.
+- Negative = internal reversal/gap or distance between separate objects of the same color only.
+- Distances across different colors are never negative elements.
+- Single-object minimum is checked separately when the technology defines it.
+- Antialias shades belonging to one flat color are clustered into that color.
+- Full-color / unreliable separation becomes manual, never fake automatic morphology.
+- Corner/junction tapers are filtered; sustained thin runs and stable narrow channels remain violations.
+- Issue circles have no central dot/cross. Their physical diameter equals the corresponding minimum allowed element/gap size and the center is the detected problem center.
+
+## Preflight scope
+- Live fonts are forbidden only inside the actual artwork. Fonts in templates or outside the application field are ignored.
+- Gradients, transparency and effects inside artwork are forbidden/checked structurally.
+- Color model is checked per printing method. Pure CMYK black/white are universally allowed where established; colored CMYK/Pantone rules remain method-specific.
+- If the color model cannot be determined reliably (especially Quick Check SVG/PDF transport), require manual verification rather than inventing CMYK/Pantone data.
+
+## UI / evidence requirements
+- Header: PrintCheck + small version on one line; read-only indication retained.
+- Queue button: «Заказы ожидающие проверку».
+- Result tree: order → article → brief checklist → detailed checklist. Heavy evidence is lazy-loaded.
+- Key visual evidence is large and opens fullscreen with zoom.
+- All user-facing messages use one visual language: green success, red error, orange warning/manual, blue information; important text is separated into readable paragraphs.
+- Status marks use one fixed visual size: 8sp text, 116×27dp top badge, 18dp inline checklist status; no autosize for status labels.
+
+## Brief report requirements
+The brief report must put the important production facts at the top:
+- printing method;
+- place;
+- field W×H mm;
+- found artwork W×H mm;
+- original/downloaded/used file names for layout, selected application PDF, constructor/reference;
+- Quick Check source template, source artwork and generated ready_layout.svg.
+
+## Quick Check workflow
+Quick Check is not the old embedded-site flow. It is:
+1. Load a PDF/SVG template containing the chosen application field(s).
+2. Load artwork as SVG/PNG/JPG/WEBP.
+3. In the SVG editor choose/detect the field, inspect physical field size, place and scale artwork, and show artwork W×H plus X/Y in mm.
+4. Support fit/center, field switching and manual field rectangle correction.
+5. Save the production artifact as ready_layout.svg to Downloads/PrintCheck.
+6. Optionally run the same technical checks through normalized PDF transport while marking unreliable CMYK/Pantone as manual.
+
+## Current verified baseline inherited from alpha47
+- applicationId remains ru.printcheck.android and the persistent NON-PRODUCTION alpha signer must not change.
+- alpha47 final GitHub run 35587921299 passed audit, 135/135 core tests, Android build and signer verification.
+- alpha48 is a context/regression-lock build: no intended production-analysis algorithm change from alpha47.
